    "created_at": "2016-03-05T07:17:44Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-05T07:17:44Z",
    "body": "Also EnumerableOwnNames uses [[OwnPropertyKeys]]. I don't see a way around using [[OwnPropertyKeys]], do you? That is, the semantics described in OP cannot be done with the operations available in ECMAScript.\n\nI could see that similarly to Map/Set we might want to iterate twice. First create a list of enumerable property names and then clone them. But even then you would use [[OwnPropertyKeys]] to get the initial list, no?\n\nIs the problem instead the [[Get]]? Should that become [[GetOwnProperty]]? And then we add [[HasProperty]] for good measure in front and do the double iteration so the cloning operation cannot change the object?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
