    "created_at": "2016-03-05T15:12:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-05T15:12:39Z",
    "body": "The idea isn't to avoid [[OwnPropertyKeys]]. You still need to use that, for sure. You just need to do the [[Get]]s after checking for enumerability. Something like:\n1. Otherwise,\n   1. Let enumerableKeys be an empty List.\n   2. For each key in ? input.OPKs(),\n      1. If Type(key) is String,\n         1. Let inputDesc be ? input.GOP(k)\n         2. If inputDesc.[[Enumerable]] is true, then add key to enumerableKeys\n   3. For each key in enumerableKeys,\n      1. If ? input.HasProperty(key) is true, then:\n         1. Let inputValue be ? input.Get(key, input)\n         2. Let outputValue be ? StructuredClone(inputValue, targetRealm, memory)\n         3. Perform ? CreateDataProperty(output, key, outputValue).\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
